# Portable Windows release and publication pipeline
Workstream-ID: lea-12
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/12
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed Windows packaging and release engineering scope
Status: DONE
Milestone: Downloadable Windows desktop application with repeatable releases
Dependencies: lea-11

## Purpose
Deliver a versioned Windows x64 desktop distribution that starts from an EXE
without requiring a Python installation. Publish reviewed application assets
through a trusted-ref, least-permission GitHub Actions release pipeline.

## Tasks
- [x] Separate bundled read-only resources from private writable runtime data.
- [x] Add windowed and console entrypoints sharing one bundled runtime.
- [x] Package explicit public resources, licenses, checksums and usage instructions.
- [x] Keep installed Edge/Chrome external; disclose Chromium and optional-feature requirements.
- [x] Add validation and Windows release jobs without workstation credentials or recurring tracking.
- [x] Audit the publication tree and assets for private/runtime material.
- [x] Exercise the packaged GUI and CLI locally without submitting applications.
- [x] Publish a version tag and release; verify the exact hosted run and downloaded asset.
- [x] Record measured download/extracted sizes and remaining qualification limits.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] A real Windows EXE opens the desktop app and can invoke bundled CLI commands.
- [x] First launch creates only missing example files in a writable per-user workspace.
- [x] Upgrades do not overwrite existing configuration, answers, databases or browser profiles.
- [x] The downloadable payload excludes private context, real configurations and runtime artifacts.
- [x] Release jobs use reviewed immutable action revisions and only necessary token permissions.
- [x] Published checksums match the actual downloadable Windows artifact.
- [x] Release publication is verified separately from tests and local package generation.

## Completion evidence
Published Windows x64 release:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/releases/tag/v0.2.0
The annotated tag and downloaded manifest identify exact built source
4c1fcb00afc36915d89e1ac911e5240e92ce22c7.
Main qualification succeeded:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/actions/runs/42422898194
Tag qualification and publication both succeeded:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/actions/runs/42423476175
Hosted checks passed Ruff, scoped Black (112 files), product mypy (69 files),
681 tests, Windows packaging and frozen offline smoke. Official actionlint
1.7.12 also validates the workflow.

The actual downloaded ZIP is 114488935 bytes (109.2 MiB); its 449 installed
files total 267371296 bytes (255.0 MiB). ZIP SHA256:
a07e7cfcdb0e14d907e9f9c16491af908708a2862bd1a8ba704e008e90cc7f8c
All three downloaded assets match GitHub's published sizes and SHA256 digests.
SHA256SUMS, the version/source manifest and all per-file hashes were verified
before and after installation. The earlier 106.0/245.5 MiB working-tree build
was not substituted for the hosted release.

Offline smoke against the actual installed release passed version/help/init,
test-form, statistics, CSV/XLSX export, existing-config preservation, GUI
rendering, Playwright driver startup and GUI-to-console child execution.
A normal native desktop launch opened a responsive window and closed cleanly;
the example-only default workspace and non-overwriting shortcut were verified.
Python is bundled; installed Edge/Chrome remain external.

Original Qt, Loguru and et-xmlfile notices are enforced by regression tests.
Tracked private continuity, mixed legacy notes and answer-quality runtime
reports were removed from the public tip without deleting local files.
The release is unsigned. Fresh-machine execution, live LinkedIn submission
and human aesthetic acceptance remain separate, unperformed qualifications.
No private configuration or browser profile was migrated by installation.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-08: Verified repository owner access and workflow scope without printing
  credentials. No prior release or tag was present. Selected a portable folder
  rather than a self-extracting one-file binary; browser binaries stay external.
- 2026-11-08: Added exact-commit manifests, SHA256SUMS, pinned Actions and
  tag-only publication with job-scoped permissions. Local frozen smoke exposed
  and resolved embedded-interpreter encoding and SQLite cleanup defects.
- 2026-11-08: Completed notice provenance and public-tree review. Original
  et-xmlfile MIT and Python-derived-code licenses were copied byte-for-byte
  from the SHA256-verified official source archive; missing notices fail the build.
- 2026-11-08: Initial hosted run 42422527663 failed at test collection because
  dashboard test dependencies were absent. Added the dashboard extra to CI;
  corrected exact-source main and tag qualifications passed all 681 tests.
- 2026-11-08: Published v0.2.0, downloaded all three actual assets, verified
  checksums and all 449 files, and installed without overwriting an existing
  version. The installed frozen smoke and normal native startup both passed.
  No new LinkedIn application or invitation was attempted.
